  "notes": "Agent re-read after the Code Health refactor, 2026-11-07, under the owner directive transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/agent-rereview-after-refactor-2026-11-07.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only. Read conformance.audit_vocabulary_drift and core.audit_vocabulary. mcp-re-core/src/audit.rs, audit/ and error.rs have no diff. The guard test mcp-re-conformance/tests/audit_vocabulary_guard_test.rs was split into corpus.rs, producers.rs, source.rs and vocabulary.rs. I compared the old 816-line file with the new five: the same 13 test functions exist; the expected event-set constants, CRATE_SOURCE_TREES, NOT_SCANNED, TARGET_TABLE, CRATE_KINDS, COMPILED_SOURCE_DIRS and SOLE_MINTING_FILES are identical; frozen_wire_codes, production_literals, the slice and event_type const parsers, the quote-pair literal scanner, minting_files, crate_packages, the carrier and projection checks (six carriers, the two From<&_> for McpReError signatures, the wildcard-arm refusal) and the anti-vacuity floors (at least 15 frozen tokens, invalid_signature present, every pinned event in the production region) keep the same predicates and refusals. The execution and accounting category checks are one assert_own_category helper over the same slices and the same other-category disjointness lists. The claim holds. The mutation lane was not run, and no test was run. Evidence class as registered (V0).",
